            <ArticleTitle>Diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis: Forestier's disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>375-82; quiz 383-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Diffuse idiopathic skeletal hyperostosis (DISH) or Forestier's disease is characterized by calcification and ossification of soft tissue entheses of ligaments and tendons. DISH is believed to be a variant of osteoarthritis (OA) without the degenerative intervertebral disc and joint degenerative qualities seen in classic OA. The likely pathoetiologic causes of DISH are presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
